erved running artifacts, so a changed prompt, model, weights | The id is computed from the manifest file (identity.py:63-75), not from observed running artifacts, so a drifted prompt, model or tool setup still emi\n NO C03.5 app/startup.py:43 | A mismatch blocks or quarantines the deployment, not only logs it. | Mismatch is only logged; startup_checks goes on to compute and return the id and the app starts (startup.py:44-46, main.py:83).\n== C04 gap Detect drift per agent\n viol ['Compare running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies'] also ['C03']\n sum No per-deployment drift check exists beyond a one-time startup comparison that covers few categories and only logs.\n RF app/startup.py:43 Detected drift is only logged and the process continues.\n NO C04.1 app/startup.py:31 | A drift check compares running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network polic | The only comparison is the startup check: image, prompts, policy/tools hash and model ids. It does not compare MCP server lists, permissions (RBAC/IAM\n NO C04.2 app/main.py:83 | The drift check runs per agent deployment, on a schedule or on change events. | The comparison runs once at process start. No cron, scheduled CI job or change-event trigger runs a drift check in this repo (ci.yaml triggers only on\n NO C04.3 app/startup.py:43 | Detected drift triggers an alert and a set response (block, quarantine, or rollback) defined in config, with a | Drift only logs; there is no alert, no block/quarantine/rollback response in config and no time limit.\n== C05 gap Control dependency, model, and training changes\n viol ['Pin dependency versions'] also []\n sum Direct dependencies are pinned but there is no lockfile, so transitive packages are unpinned.\n RF Dockerfile:7 Transitive dependencies are not locked; no lockfile or hashes.\n NO C05.1 Dockerfile:7 | Dependency versions are pinned with exact versions or hashes in lockfiles, with no rang