e call is blocked. | The release-manifest check of policy, tools config, prompts, image and models only logs on mismatch; startup continues and serves. A failed required i\n NO E06.5 app/identity.py:95 | Under MCP 2026-07-28, relevant header/body mismatches are rejected before routing or policy relies on them, an | Private token cache is keyed by audience, scope and tenant only. It omits the verified subject, agent instance and policy version, so one user's deleg\n== E08 gap Bounded delegated authority\n viol ['Give sub-agents only the powers approved for their task'] also []\n sum The extractor sub-agent falls back to the parent's full tool set and shares the parent's cached tokens, so its authority is not narrowed to its task.\n RF app/extractor.py:25 EXTRACTOR_ROLE 'line_item_extractor' does not exist in config/tools.yaml (role is 'extractor'), so the sub-agent silently gets the parent's full procurement tool set\n NO E08.1 app/tools/__init__.py:69 | Each child gets a credential narrowed to its approved task (for example by token exchange or transaction token | The child runs as role 'line_item_extractor' (extractor.py:25) but tools.yaml defines only 'extractor', so the lookup falls back to the full 'procurem\n== E09 gap Recursive shutdown\n viol ['Check that the stop reaches every descendant within the set time'] also []\n sum The kill switch is checked only when a run starts, so a halt does not stop running agents, their children or their open calls, and nothing revokes their tokens.\n RF app/killswitch.py:25 assert_running is called only at run start (loop.py:127); halts do not stop running agents or sub-agents\n NO E09.1 app/loop.py:127 | A stop signal from the root reaches every descendant: nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open t | The halt flag is read once, at run start. The model loop (loop.py:139), tool dispatch (loop.py:53) and the extractor child loop (extractor.py:64) neve\n NO E09.2 app/identity.py:97 | Stopping revokes descendants' 