{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019rX7k6n8xuTxz9pbCqQAgf","type":"tool_result","content":"skill/references/agent.md:34:### Not covered here\nskill/references/agent.md:98:### Not covered here\nskill/references/agent.md:170:### Not covered here\n# Independent coverage discovery: E07 — Untrusted peer messages\n\nEstablish your own findings from the code before comparing with any earlier\nreview. You are not told the earlier rating, answers, citations or exceptions.\n**Requirement:** Authenticate the sending agent (prove its identity) on every message, even validly signed ones. Validate message types and schemas, and check what that peer is allowed to ask for. Where a replay could repeat an action, check freshness and track nonces or request IDs. Checking the sender alone doesn't stop replays. Test faked identity, replayed requests, requests across tenants, and instructions passed along by a compromised peer. Verify signed agent cards where they exist. A card says who an agent is, not what it may do. Check callback and webhook URLs against SSRF. A valid sender doesn't make a message's content trusted.\n**N/A condition:** The agent receives no messages from other agents (no A2A server, peer endpoint, or agent-to-agent channel).\n\nInventory all relevant paths/fields, including indirect paths, helpers and both directions of\nhandoffs. For each check, record coverage rows (subject, status enforced/missing/\nunclear/not_applicable, evidence, exact quote, note), deviations (required-control\nomissions; empty only if none), and concrete falsification attempts (category,\ninput, trace, outcome blocked/accepted/unclear/not_applicable, evidence, quote).\nSmall or residual omissions are still omissions. A missing row or unresolved\ncoverage cannot support holds. Do not run repository code; derive counterexamples\nby tracing it. A bounded_after budget claim needs a finite overshoot bound, not\njust a shared counter. Exemptions need quoted scope evidence.\n\nSet applicability absent/present/unclear, with top-level evidence, quote and a\nsearch explanation. Absent must satisfy the exact N/A condition. When present,\nverdict is failed if any required check fails, unclear if any is unresolved,\notherwise upheld. Copy broken words from the requirement into violates.\n\n\n## E07.1\n\n**Check:** Every peer message is authenticated to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find the handler for incoming peer messages (A2A server, peer endpoint). 2) Check each message is authenticated to a specific sending agent (mTLS identity, verified token subject). 3) Answer no if any route accepts unauthenticated messages, trusts a self-declared sender field, or accepts any valid signature without mapping it to a known agent.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## E07.2\n\n**Check:** Message types and schemas are validated, and each request is checked against what that peer is allowed to ask for, including tenant.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open the peer message handler. 2) Check message type and schema validation. 3) Check a per-peer allowlist of request types and tenants, keyed on the authenticated sender. 4) Answer no if schemas are unchecked, any authenticated peer can ask for anything, or tenant is taken from the message body.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## E07.3\n\n**Check:** Action requests carry a nonce or request ID and a freshness check, and replays are rejected or do not repeat side effects.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find action request handling. 2) Check for a nonce or request ID plus a freshness (timestamp) check, with seen IDs stored. 3) Answer no if no replay check exists, the nonce is never stored or compared, or a repeated ID repeats side effects.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## E07.4\n\n**Check:** Peer message content is handled as untrusted data and is not placed into system or instruction prompts.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Trace peer message content to the prompt builder. 2) Check it goes into user or tool-result content as untrusted data. 3) Answer no if any path places it into the system prompt or an instruction template.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04ff3a3b-8cb7-48a0-b868-00dd7067b169","uuid":"0b521fd1-6545-4606-98a6-bec4f6e7cf87","timestamp":"2026-10-20T16:30:57.071Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"skill/references/agent.md:34:### Not covered here\nskill/references/agent.md:98:### Not covered here\nskill/references/agent.md:170:### Not covered here\n# Independent coverage discovery: E07 — Untrusted peer messages\n\nEstablish your own findings from the code before comparing with any earlier\nreview. You are not told the earlier rating, answers, citations or exceptions.\n**Requirement:** Authenticate the sending agent (prove its identity) on every message, even validly signed ones. Validate message types and schemas, and check what that peer is allowed to ask for. Where a replay could repeat an action, check freshness and track nonces or request IDs. Checking the sender alone doesn't stop replays. Test faked identity, replayed requests, requests across tenants, and instructions passed along by a compromised peer. Verify signed agent cards where they exist. A card says who an agent is, not what it may do. Check callback and webhook URLs against SSRF. A valid sender doesn't make a message's content trusted.\n**N/A condition:** The agent receives no messages from other agents (no A2A server, peer endpoint, or agent-to-agent channel).\n\nInventory all relevant paths/fields, including indirect paths, helpers and both directions of\nhandoffs. For each check, record coverage rows (subject, status enforced/missing/\nunclear/not_applicable, evidence, exact quote, no